{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For I will dispossess nations from before you and I will widen your border.</b> Since it is a time of favor, I will widen your border beyond what I gave to Abraham, namely the land of Sihon and Og, for I gave him only from the Jordan eastward. Therefore <b>no man will covet your land</b> — this land that I have widened for you, even though you cross the Jordan for the pilgrimage festival and the cities remain without inhabitants. For they will say: those who were already established — HaShem dispossessed them from before them; all the more so we cannot conquer their land, since they are occupied with His commandments."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:52.227811917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}